{
 "name": "vent_lamp_leak",
 "saveFile": "minimal_colony.rws",
 "description": "Lamp light must NOT cross a Vent in an exterior wall, and this pins that it does not. Two sealed 11x11 roofed boxes at (-13,25) and (13,25), a TorchLamp three cells north of the south wall in each, midnight so the torches are the only light in the frame. The control's south wall is unbroken granite; the test room has a core Vent in the middle of its south wall. Vent is blockLight=true, so vanilla's glow flood refuses to cross it and every blocker test in this mod reads it as solid. Written while chasing a report of light coming through vents: it came back CLEAN, in both the gameplay light (*_out_glow, equal to the control within run-to-run drift) and the composed overlay (*_out_rendered, 0 on both), with vector lighting on and off -- which is what identified the real leak as the sky path (NativeSkyFalloffGrid.BlocksFlood) rather than the lamp path. Kept as a regression test because a future change to the vector polygon or the mask could open exactly this. The *_in_* pins exist because two dark cells outside prove nothing if the rooms were dark too. Clouds off explicitly, Realistic preset.",
